u]}$ denotes $ rac{1}{2} (\partial_{\mu} A_{
u} - \partial_{
u} A_{\mu})$. Thus, the formula states that the electromagnetic field tensor is precisely this antisymmetric combination of gradients of the electromagnetic four-potential, $A_{\mu}$. The four-potential $A_{\mu}$ is a four-vector composed of the scalar potential $\phi$ and the magnetic vector potential $\mathbf{A}$ as $A^\mu = ( rac{\phi}{c}, \mathbf{A})$. The components of $F_{\mu
